# Build-context exclusions for the repo-root Dockerfile.
#
# The compose build context became the repository root in issue #445, so this
# file is load-bearing: without it every `docker compose build` uploads the git
# history, the Ralph worktrees (each a full second checkout) and every local
# cache before reading a single instruction.
#
# WHAT IS DELIBERATELY *NOT* EXCLUDED: `tests/`. The deployment's paper-exchange
# books (`tests/fixtures/books/deep_walk`) and forecast cassette
# (`tests/fixtures/forecast/cassettes.json`) live there and are the fixtures the
# shipped `pipeline` service names, so excluding it would produce an image that
# builds cleanly and then dies on a missing fixture. That coupling is asserted
# by tests/deploy/test_deployment_launches_paper.py rather than left to comment.

# Version control and agent scratch state.
.git
.gitattributes
.github
.ralph
.claude
plan
plans
git-issues
prompts

# Local caches and build/test output.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.hypothesis
htmlcov
coverage.xml
.coverage
*.egg-info
build
dist
.venv
venv
